                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Let me start off by saying that £2.49 for [i]this[/i] is an absolute outrage.\n\nIt's an extremely short single-screen platformer where you collect candy and travel through a crypt to get to the next level. You need to collect all the candy on each level to progress to the next.\n\nThe hitboxes for the character and the platforms are awfully tedious to work with (I died multiple times because my character got stuck on a ledge and fell), which leads to having to relearn everything you know about platformers just to get up on one ledge.\n\nThe graphics aren't great, either. They look cheaply made (Or sourced from some sort of image library), which further adds to the fact this game isn't worth its asking price.\n\nThe music is definitely sourced from Pixabay as I'm sure I've heard it before, which again detracts from the value.\n\nOverall, don't buy this game. Save your £2.49 and buy something else.",
